1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:02,180
One major country breaks the pattern of

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:03,067
its peers.

3
00:00:03,067 --> 00:00:04,742
It is not the one you'd guess.

4
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:07,405
China, India, or Nigeria.

5
00:00:07,405 --> 00:00:09,405
One of these giants has surprisingly low

6
00:00:09,405 --> 00:00:10,292
access.

7
00:00:10,767 --> 00:00:12,292
It counts any home with a sink,

8
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:14,292
bucket, or basin, as long as there

9
00:00:14,292 --> 00:00:15,142
is soap.

10
00:00:15,642 --> 00:00:18,217
China has 95.3 percent.

11
00:00:18,217 --> 00:00:20,305
Almost every rural home there has soap

12
00:00:20,305 --> 00:00:21,492
and water ready.

13
00:00:21,992 --> 00:00:24,530
India has 85.9 percent.

14
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:27,142
That is 26 times the value Ethiopia

15
00:00:27,142 --> 00:00:27,892
has.

16
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:31,742
The outlier is Nigeria, at 22.9 percent.

17
00:00:31,742 --> 00:00:33,342
Far below its peers.

18
00:00:33,817 --> 00:00:37,067
At the bottom: Ethiopia has 3.3 percent,

19
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:39,217
and Liberia has just 1 percent.

20
00:00:39,717 --> 00:00:41,467
Does your home have a dedicated spot

21
00:00:41,467 --> 00:00:42,792
for soap and water?
